                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the target and the bias`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Voltura's defensible standalone EV is <strong>EUR 1.0B</strong> (LTM EBITDA EUR 80M × 12.5x). The sell-side guides EUR 1.5B — a <strong>50% control premium</strong> versus a European tech-M&A median of ~30%. Corporate Development's base case claims <strong>EUR 90M</strong> of run-rate synergies, but the credible band runs EUR 45M (low) to EUR 130M (bull). Build your number <em>up from standalone</em> — not down from the ask — probability-weight the synergy range, and read Brandt's memo for what it is: anchoring (“EUR 1.5B is fair”), confirmation framing, a planning-fallacy ramp, escalation and overconfidence. <em>Show me the number you'd reach if you'd never heard “1.5 billion.”</em>`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Install procedural rationality before bidding`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `This is the heart of the research. Before you commit to any number, spend a limited governance budget — <strong>9 days</strong> against the 21-day clock, plus political capital with Brandt — to install safeguards: an <strong>outside-view</strong> valuation, a <strong>pre-mortem</strong>, a ratified <strong>walk-away price</strong>, a synergy <strong>red team</strong>, and <strong>decision hygiene</strong> that separates the champion from the approver. Each costs days and friction but measurably shrinks the bias score and tightens the synergy estimate. The finding: an outside view and a pre-mortem take two days and move your premium by ten points. <em>Which is more expensive — two days, or EUR 200M of overpayment?</em>`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Set the bid premium under auction pressure`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Set the binding premium while the rival bids live. The US major opens at <strong>35%</strong>; Voltura's bankers signal <strong>55% “wins it”</strong>; Brandt pushes to “just clear them.” Each 10% premium ≈ EUR 100M; break-even needs ≈ <strong>EUR 120M</strong> of recurring synergies; below ~12% you may lose Voltura. Decide whether to <em>honor the walk-away price you set</em>, and structure terms — earn-out, contingent value right, stock-vs-cash — that hedge synergy risk while leverage climbs toward the <strong>3.0x covenant</strong>. <em>Where is your walk-away number when the bankers say one more turn wins it?</em>`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Recover: synergy capture vs the price you paid`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `The outcome is revealed — and synergies land in the low/base/bull band <strong>partly as a function of the rigor you imposed</strong>. Compute realized <strong>acquisition return</strong> and <strong>synergy-capture rate</strong>, then build a 100-day plan to defend value. Drive integration with discipline or rush to declare victory; reconcile the premium paid to value created honestly, or stay glossy to match the public commitment Brandt made. <em>Returns come from realized synergies exceeding the premium — not from winning the deal.</em>`,

                    r1_anchor_label:        `Where do you start the valuation?`,
                    anchor_standalone:      `Build up from EUR 1.0B standalone EV (12.5x EBITDA), then add probability-weighted synergies as a range`,
                    anchor_median:          `Start from the EU median ~30% premium benchmark and reason toward a defensible number`,
                    anchor_ask:             `Start from the sell-side EUR 1.5B ask and work out which synergies justify it`,
                    r1_synergy_label:       `How do you treat the EUR 45M / 90M / 130M synergy band?`,
                    syn_weighted:           `Probability-weight the range and capitalize only the credible run-rate (treat the ramp with skepticism)`,
                    syn_base:               `Capitalize the EUR 90M base case in full — that is the analyst's central estimate`,
                    syn_bull:               `Capitalize the EUR 130M bull case — Voltura is strategic and the upside is real`,
                    r1_bias_label:          `How many of the CEO memo's claims do you log as bias rather than evidence? (0–5)`,
                    r1_bias_readout:        `Claims tagged as bias in the register:`,
                    r1_bias_hint:           `The memo carries anchoring (“EUR 1.5B is fair”), confirmation framing, a planning-fallacy synergy ramp, escalation (“not losing this”), and overconfidence (“never missed a target”). Naming them is the first debiasing act.`,

                    r2_safeguard_label:     `Install procedural-rationality safeguards BEFORE bidding (each costs days & political capital; together they shrink the bias score and tighten synergies)`,
                    sg_outside:             `Outside-view / reference-class valuation (2 days)`,
                    sg_premortem:           `Structured pre-mortem — “it's 2028, the deal failed, why?” (1 day)`,
                    sg_walkaway:            `Mandated walk-away price, ratified by the Lead Independent Director (1 day)`,
