                    insight_creator:        `Disciplined value creator: you valued Voltura up from standalone, installed real safeguards, set a premium inside the break-even logic, and captured enough synergy to clear the price. Returns came from synergies exceeding the premium — exactly the calibrated judgment the research rewards.`,
                    insight_curse:          `The winner's curse: you won the auction at a premium your synergies couldn't cover, and value transferred to Voltura's sellers on day one. You won the deal and lost the shareholders — the precise outcome procedural rationality is designed to prevent.`,
                    insight_lost:           `Over-corrected: you bid below the rival and lost the one asset the CEO staked his credibility on. Debiasing isn't reflexive conservatism — it's bidding the right amount for the right reasons. Was EUR 1.0B truly your reservation value, or fear of the premium?`,
                    insight_destroyed:      `Value destroyed: realized synergies didn't exceed the premium paid, so acquisition return is negative. A tighter synergy estimate, a lower premium, or a hedged structure would have changed the math — overpayment, not strategy, drove the result.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `Mixed outcome: you captured some value but the premium absorbed most of it. The premium you pay and the rigor you impose — not the headline “win” — are what determine the return.`,
                    insight_nowalkaway:     `You won without a pre-committed walk-away price. Discipline at the moment of decision is a hope, not a constraint, unless the ceiling was ratified before the auction heated up.`,
                    insight_nohygiene:      `The deal champion was also the approver. Decision hygiene — separating the CEO who wants the deal from the board that ratifies it — is the structural antidote to escalation that your bias score still reflects.`,
                    insight_nogovernance:   `You spent none of the governance budget. The 21-day clock was real, but skipping the outside view and pre-mortem is the cheapest two days you never spent — and the most expensive overpayment you did.`,
                    insight_capture:        `Strong synergy capture: the rigor you imposed earlier raised realized synergies above the band a rushed integration would have delivered. Capture rate, not the premium headline, is where the paid premium turns into value.`,
                    insight_lowbias:        `Your decision-bias score is low — anchoring, overconfidence and escalation were all constrained by the process you built. That is the Pavićević finding in action: procedural rationality, not personality, debiases the decision.`,

                    hint_governance:        `You've spent no governance budget. An outside view and a pre-mortem take two days and move your premium by ten points — install at least the walk-away price and decision hygiene before you bid.`,
                    hint_curse:             `Your premium is in winner's-curse territory. Above ~55% you need your bull-case synergies merely to break even — re-check your walk-away line before the bankers' signal moves you again.`,
                    hint_lost:              `You bid below the rival's opening and risk losing Voltura. Debiasing isn't reflexive conservatism — confirm whether EUR 1.0B is your true reservation value or an over-correction.`,
                    hint_bias:              `Your decision-bias score is high. Anchor to standalone value, weight the synergy range, and install the walk-away price and decision hygiene — the structural safeguards that constrain escalation.`,
